    "validation_execution_closure_gate": "Protocol v5 section 9 post-closure gate: after any validation execution that ends without a completed schedule - interruption, budget stop, or lapse - no subsequent validation execution may be authorized until the closure record (cause classification, custodian logs, attestations, and the lapse explanation if any) has been independently reviewed and committed. The gate names that record, states its verdict, pins its LF-normalized digest, and names the independent review of the payload commit that set these fields; requireValidationGate refuses an otherwise-open validation gate whose last execution status is not complete until all four are set, the verdict is ACCEPT, and the named closure record reproduces the pinned digest. The runner verifies identity, not prose. Whether the closure record is an accepting independent review is a human judgment and is an OBLIGATION on the commit that sets these fields, not an assumption about one: the four fields may be set only by a payload commit independently reviewed under the freeze workflow, whose reviewer must read the named closure record and rule that it is an accepting independent review; a chair gate patch must not set them. The digest pin additionally refuses a closure record edited after the review that blessed it.",
